From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:07:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bound the all-valid fill by the entry count, not by the last index

TemplatedValidityMask::SetAllValid() fills every entry below the last
with a loop bounded by EntryCount(count) - 1, and GCC turns the loop
into a memset whose length it bounds from that expression. EntryCount()
is (count + 63) / 64, which wraps to zero for a count within 63 of the
type's maximum, so the compiler reads the index as possibly SIZE_MAX
and -Wstringop-overflow reports a memset of more than any object can
hold, twice, at the call sites it inlines. The loop now runs while
i + 1 < entry_count, which bounds the fill by the entry count itself,
and the last index is derived after it; the fill is the same for every
count the function is called with.

Only CI's GCC 15.2 raises this, in duckdb/duckdb-r#2937's check of the
v2.0 landing; GCC 13.3 and 14.2 are silent on the same tree, so the
patch is confirmed by that check rather than locally.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
 src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/types/validity_mask.hpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/types/validity_mask.hpp b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/types/validity_mask.hpp
index f3c351bf83..81815fd219 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/types/validity_mask.hpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/types/validity_mask.hpp
@@ -305,10 +305,11 @@ public:
 		if (count == 0) {
 			return;
 		}
-		auto last_entry_index = ValidityBuffer::EntryCount(count) - 1;
-		for (idx_t i = 0; i < last_entry_index; i++) {
+		const auto entry_count = ValidityBuffer::EntryCount(count);
+		for (idx_t i = 0; i + 1 < entry_count; i++) {
 			validity_mask[i] = ValidityBuffer::MAX_ENTRY;
 		}
+		const auto last_entry_index = entry_count - 1;
 		auto last_entry_bits = count % BITS_PER_VALUE;
 		validity_mask[last_entry_index] |= (last_entry_bits == 0)
 		                                       ? ValidityBuffer::MAX_ENTRY
